From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:02:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Keep the origin of a media resource when its fetch
 restarts

Every fetch of a media element started out origin-clean, until the
headers of its response arrived. A fetch that restarts the fetch of the
same media resource, after a seek or once the player needs data again,
therefore made a video that was fetched in no-cors mode from another
origin count as origin-clean for as long as the server took to answer,
so that drawing it to a canvas or into an ImageBitmap did not taint
them.

Start such a fetch with the origin-clean flag of the fetch that it
replaces, and keep the flag false once a response of the resource was
not CORS-same-origin. A new resource selection still starts with a
fresh flag.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: a new WPT test draws a video from another origin, fetched
without CORS, to a canvas while it seeks, from a server that delays
its answer to a range request that starts past byte 0.

Validation: the new test fails in 3 of 3 runs without this patch, where getImageData returns the pixels of the video while it seeks, and passes in 3 of 3 with it. drawing-images-to-the-canvas and imagebitmap (43 tests): on ohos-main only the new test fails, and all pass with the series. `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 6 --timeout-multiplier 2` of html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements, the-video-element, and html/canvas/element/manual/drawing-images-to-the-canvas and imagebitmap (475 tests) with the series up to the last patch: no new failure; the unexpected results (media_fragment_seek, autoplay-default-permissions-policy, load-removes-queued-error-event) also occur on ohos-main. `./mach check --ohos` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
